// The length-encoded integer of the MySQL client/server protocol:
// https://dev.mysql.com/doc/dev/mysql-server/latest/page_protocol_basic_dt_integers.html
//
// One octet under 251, otherwise a marker saying how many little-endian octets follow.
// The gap it leaves at the top is deliberate: 0xfb is NULL in a row and 0xff begins an
// error packet, so neither can be mistaken for a length. MariaDB writes the same.
